- * high).  GICv2 maps SPI n to interrupt ID n + 32.  Only the MBOX line is
- * wired in this first patch (see the .c); ALIVE and WDOG are recorded for the
- * next session.  The first interrupt cell of each triple is 0 == SPI.
+ * high).  The first interrupt cell of each triple is 0 == SPI.  On this board
+ * the GIC is a GIC-400 driven as a non-secure GICv2 (pexpert/arm/pe_fiq.c,
+ * "Exynos7580 GIC-400" block), and GICv2 maps SPI n to interrupt ID n + 32.
+ *
+ * None of the three lines is enabled by this port.  The mailbox is serviced by
+ * polling INTMSR0 from a thread instead: XNU's arm64 IRQ entry hands every
+ * "other" interrupt to the single per-CPU handler installed by
+ * ml_install_interrupt_handler(), which on this tree belongs to
+ * IOCPUInterruptController (iokit/Kernel/IOCPU.cpp:626-640), so a BSD driver
